      "id": "dp:1",
      "label": "DP-01",
      "source": "corpus/canon/resources/design-principles.md",
      "start": 5,
      "text": "## 1. Honor the executing workflow's inherited destination\n\nA leaf technique's Destination declaration must satisfy the Rules of the ancestor TECHNIQUE.md in its executing workflow's techniques directory. This fixture executes produce through qualification's run activity and deliver routine, so it inherits qualification/techniques/TECHNIQUE.md. Compare the leaf's destination value with the inherited required value. The ancestor's constraint is a declaration, not a conflicting leaf destination. Files without a leaf destination declaration are not independently checked for this principle; explicit call and inheritance relationships must carry the rule to the leaf instance.\n",
      "title": "1. Honor the executing workflow's inherited destination"
    }
  },
